WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.534
-One of those things
you always say.

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:06.901
You always say to yourself what?
-Oh, gosh. I say...

00:00:06.901 --> 00:00:09.200
If you're going to eat gravy,

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:10.701
don't leave it
in your soul patch.

00:00:10.701 --> 00:00:12.467
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:12.467 --> 00:00:14.267
That's one that's
always gone down.

00:00:14.267 --> 00:00:20.667
[ Laughter ]

00:00:20.667 --> 00:00:22.467
Where I come from,
everyone says that.

00:00:22.467 --> 00:00:24.100
If you're going to eat gravy,

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:25.367
don't leave it
in your soul patch.

00:00:25.367 --> 00:00:27.133
-That's right.
-But what if you're eating,

00:00:27.133 --> 00:00:28.868
for instance,
a chicken cordon bleu?

00:00:28.868 --> 00:00:30.100
[ Laughter ]

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:32.067
That has
some type of thing on there.

00:00:32.067 --> 00:00:34.467
You can get something like that.
But that's a good food.

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:37.534
I mean, you you love to go out.
You love to eat.

00:00:37.534 --> 00:00:39.234
-I tell you what, I do.
I love to eat.

00:00:39.234 --> 00:00:43.067
I love the outdoors.
I mean, honestly, this year,

00:00:43.067 --> 00:00:44.567
like towards the end
of the year, I need a break.

00:00:44.567 --> 00:00:48.934
What I plan to do
is just go out.

00:00:48.934 --> 00:00:50.434
Um...
[ Laughter ]

00:00:50.434 --> 00:00:53.734
I want to --
I want to get a fishing rod

00:00:53.734 --> 00:00:57.067
and I want to go out. I want to
eat some -- I want to --

00:00:57.067 --> 00:00:59.367
I just want to eat
a peanut butter jelly...fish.

00:00:59.367 --> 00:01:01.234
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:01.234 --> 00:01:03.968
♪♪

00:01:03.968 --> 00:01:05.167
Peanut butter jelly...

00:01:05.167 --> 00:01:07.834
-Peanut butter jelly/fish.

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:09.200
Yeah.
-Fish.

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:10.801
-That's what you want to do.
Yeah.

00:01:10.801 --> 00:01:11.868
Peanut butter and jelly
and fish.

00:01:11.868 --> 00:01:14.267
-Or hunt jellyfish.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.267 --> 00:01:16.467
-Just hunt jellyfish.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.467 --> 00:01:17.868
I don't think you hunt j--

00:01:17.868 --> 00:01:19.734
Do you hunt jellyfish?

00:01:19.734 --> 00:01:21.167
-You can hunt anything.

00:01:21.167 --> 00:01:24.133
-I can't eat peanut butter
and jelly sandwiches,

00:01:24.133 --> 00:01:26.567
so it's a sore subject for me.
-Oh, I'm really sorry.

00:01:26.567 --> 00:01:29.334
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.334 --> 00:01:30.667
What can you eat?

00:01:30.667 --> 00:01:33.801
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.801 --> 00:01:35.567
-You say why -- You say,
why can't I eat them?

00:01:35.567 --> 00:01:38.100
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:39.167
-Yeah. Why?

00:01:39.167 --> 00:01:40.868
Why can't you eat
a peanut butter jelly?

00:01:40.868 --> 00:01:44.968
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.968 --> 00:01:45.968
-Dentures.

00:01:45.968 --> 00:01:47.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.901 --> 00:01:52.634
♪♪

00:01:52.634 --> 00:01:54.434
Chris Pratt, good to see you
again, my friend.

00:01:54.434 --> 00:01:56.701
-Nice to see you.
-You look sharp. You look great.

00:01:56.701 --> 00:01:58.567
-Yeah, It's a suit.
-Yeah, it is.

00:01:58.567 --> 00:02:00.100
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:02.667
-Was the first time we met?
Was it here?

00:02:02.667 --> 00:02:04.834
-No.
You know, the first time we met.

00:02:04.834 --> 00:02:06.601
You're never going
to remember this.

00:02:06.601 --> 00:02:07.834
-Was it September 3rd?

00:02:07.834 --> 00:02:09.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:11.534
-On Third Street.
-Yes.

00:02:11.534 --> 00:02:16.868
-It was during -- It was --
I just got started in Hollywood.

00:02:16.868 --> 00:02:19.100
I worked on a TV show.

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:22.000
I got nominated for something
called the Best Sidekick

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:24.167
for like a Teen Choice Awards.

00:02:24.167 --> 00:02:26.868
It was a really big deal to me.
I got to take a limo.

00:02:26.868 --> 00:02:29.934
It was like all so new
and novel still.

00:02:29.934 --> 00:02:32.334
And I had this little bit where
I was like pres-- I didn't win.

00:02:32.334 --> 00:02:35.267
The point is, I got nominated
for a Teen Choice Award.

00:02:35.267 --> 00:02:38.033
-We get it. You're a big star.
-[ Claps ]

00:02:38.033 --> 00:02:38.968
-Yeah, yeah, yeah. We get it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:38.968 --> 00:02:41.067
-Oh, yes. Come on. Yes. Yes.

00:02:41.067 --> 00:02:42.467
That's really not the point.

00:02:42.467 --> 00:02:45.701
The point really
was that afterwards I did

00:02:45.701 --> 00:02:47.968
like this little comedy bit
and presented,

00:02:47.968 --> 00:02:49.934
and it kind of went
over all right,

00:02:49.934 --> 00:02:53.234
but you came up to me
at the end of it and you said,

00:02:53.234 --> 00:02:56.501
"Hey, man, great job tonight.
You were really funny tonight."

00:02:56.501 --> 00:02:59.567
And it meant so much to me.

00:02:59.567 --> 00:03:02.100
It was just so nice to have
someone, like --

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:04.067
[ Audience awws ]
No, really, truly.

00:03:04.067 --> 00:03:05.734
Yeah, it was --
-That's cool.

00:03:05.734 --> 00:03:08.167
-It was cool
and it just meant a lot to me

00:03:08.167 --> 00:03:10.033
because, like, you know,
I knew you from "SNL"

00:03:10.033 --> 00:03:12.634
and I knew that you made
a living doing funny things.

00:03:12.634 --> 00:03:14.000
And I wanted
to make people laugh.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:17.300
And it just really meant a lot.
And I think it's cool.

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:18.834
I just think you deserve
all your success

00:03:18.834 --> 00:03:21.534
because you were nice to me
and nice people deserve success.

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:24.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:24.868 --> 00:03:26.467
-I want to say
congratulations to you.

00:03:26.467 --> 00:03:27.934
It couldn't happen
to a better guy.

00:03:27.934 --> 00:03:29.767
Gosh, all these fun
things are happening.

00:03:29.767 --> 00:03:32.167
You're doing the new
Jurassic Park movie.

00:03:32.167 --> 00:03:33.601
-Yes.
-That's amazing.

00:03:33.601 --> 00:03:35.234
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah. Thanks, man.

00:03:35.234 --> 00:03:36.367
Thanks.
-That's exciting.

00:03:36.367 --> 00:03:39.701
-Yeah, I'm excited.
I'm really excited.

00:03:39.701 --> 00:03:41.067
Yeah. Jurassic Park.

00:03:41.067 --> 00:03:42.834
-And they're filming it
in Hawaii, right?

00:03:42.834 --> 00:03:44.601
-Whoo!
-Yes. Yeah.

00:03:44.601 --> 00:03:46.901
-That's the bad part.
-Yeah, that's gonna be tough.

00:03:46.901 --> 00:03:48.667
They're filming in Hawaii.

00:03:48.667 --> 00:03:50.267
Last time I was in Hawaii,
I lived in a van.

00:03:50.267 --> 00:03:53.300
Now I'm going back.
I'm the star of Jurassic Park.

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:54.667
-That is so awesome.
-It's gonna be great.

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:56.400
-It is the best country
in the whole wide world.

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:57.567
I love America.
-I'm moving back to the van.

00:03:57.567 --> 00:03:58.934
I'm going to have them
rent the van out.

00:03:58.934 --> 00:04:00.267
I'm moving in with my family.

00:04:00.267 --> 00:04:02.100
-Didn't you work at a Bubba
Gump Shrimp Company?

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:04.534
-Yeah, Bubba Gump
Shrimp Company in Maui.

00:04:04.534 --> 00:04:05.868
I worked there.

00:04:05.868 --> 00:04:07.334
-That's one of my
favorite theme restaurants.

00:04:07.334 --> 00:04:08.767
-It's the best theme.

00:04:08.767 --> 00:04:10.267
It's one of my
favorite theme restaurants, too.

00:04:10.267 --> 00:04:12.434
-Do you have to ask
Forrest Gump trivia to people?

00:04:12.434 --> 00:04:14.567
-Oh, yeah. That was
one of the conceptual musts.

00:04:14.567 --> 00:04:15.667
-Yes.
-Yeah.

00:04:15.667 --> 00:04:16.934
-Is that what they call them?

00:04:16.934 --> 00:04:18.367
-Yeah, yeah. There were
four of them, I think.

00:04:18.367 --> 00:04:19.767
-Do you remember any of
the trivia questions at all?

00:04:19.767 --> 00:04:21.167
-Oh, yeah. Yeah.

00:04:21.167 --> 00:04:26.767
What did Forrest Gump
drink when he met the president?

00:04:26.767 --> 00:04:28.567
-Oh, I remember.
He drank like a bunch of them.

00:04:28.567 --> 00:04:30.767
Dr Pepper?
-Dr Peppers.

00:04:30.767 --> 00:04:31.801
-Yeah!

00:04:31.801 --> 00:04:34.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:34.067 --> 00:04:38.133
-The folks at Lego
made something for you.

00:04:38.133 --> 00:04:39.334
-They did?
-Yeah.

00:04:39.334 --> 00:04:40.734
And we're going
to give it to you.

00:04:40.734 --> 00:04:41.734
I've been asked to give it
to you.

00:04:41.734 --> 00:04:42.934
-That's very nice.

00:04:42.934 --> 00:04:45.434
-So I think they said
it's maybe back here.

00:04:45.434 --> 00:04:48.000
Okay. I think I might get it.
Okay.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:50.868
Don't look. Don't look. Okay.
-Oh, wow.

00:04:50.868 --> 00:04:54.200
-To commemorate this big moment
for you, Jimmy,

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:55.334
and going to
"The Tonight Show,"

00:04:55.334 --> 00:04:56.934
the folks at Lego made this
for you.

00:04:56.934 --> 00:05:03.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:03.501 --> 00:05:04.968
-I love it.
-Isn't that cool?

00:05:06.267 --> 00:05:07.767
-I was kind of like
the Lorne Michaels

00:05:07.767 --> 00:05:09.200
of the leadership class.
I was like,

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:11.234
"All right, guys,
this one goes in.

00:05:11.234 --> 00:05:13.033
This one is cut,
this one stays."

00:05:13.033 --> 00:05:15.200
And I would sort of be
in charge of the assemblies.

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:16.567
-You would do skits for people?

00:05:16.567 --> 00:05:19.033
-We would do skits for people
in front of the school.

00:05:19.033 --> 00:05:21.734
And by the end of the week,
it would always be

00:05:21.734 --> 00:05:23.701
the same thing,
which was just a skit

00:05:23.701 --> 00:05:25.868
starring me that I'd ripped off
from "SNL" the week before.

00:05:25.868 --> 00:05:27.267
[ Laughter ]

00:05:27.267 --> 00:05:29.234
-Word for word?
-Yeah. Yes.

00:05:29.234 --> 00:05:32.868
Like, with giving "SNL"
no credit.

00:05:32.868 --> 00:05:34.133
-No, no, no. Yeah.
-Just being like,

00:05:34.133 --> 00:05:36.267
"Come on, guys. I came up
with something last night.

00:05:36.267 --> 00:05:37.300
Let's just go for it.

00:05:37.300 --> 00:05:39.667
It's called
a cheerleader sketch.

00:05:39.667 --> 00:05:41.868
I'm gonna play like
a gregarious cheerleader.

00:05:41.868 --> 00:05:44.133
Chrissy Barr, you're going
to play my sidekick.

00:05:44.133 --> 00:05:45.767
And then this is
what it looks like."

00:05:45.767 --> 00:05:47.300
They're like, "Uh, yeah.
From 'SNL,'

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:49.400
the Will Ferrell-Cheri Oteri.'"
-So I'll be playing Cheri Oteri

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:50.934
and you'll be playing
Will Ferrell.

00:05:50.934 --> 00:05:52.534
-"I don't know
what you're talking about.

00:05:52.534 --> 00:05:54.267
All right, guys,
we're on in three, two."

00:05:54.267 --> 00:05:55.667
And they're like...
-And then it worked.

00:05:55.667 --> 00:05:57.100
And now look where you are.

00:05:57.100 --> 00:05:58.767
-Now I'm doing the real show.

00:05:58.767 --> 00:06:00.501
-Oh, it's so exciting. I cannot
wait. I'm so happy for you.

00:06:00.501 --> 00:06:02.667
-And it's just as fun as when I
did it in high school.

00:06:02.667 --> 00:06:05.400
-I mean, it is, right?
-Yeah. Yeah, I think.

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:06.634
-Hey, I want to know.

00:06:06.634 --> 00:06:08.367
I want to know
about this guy here.

00:06:08.367 --> 00:06:10.367
I saw you. Who's this guy?

00:06:10.367 --> 00:06:14.701
[ Cheers, whistling
and applause ]

00:06:14.701 --> 00:06:16.667
I just have to know
the story behind it.

00:06:16.667 --> 00:06:21.133
I want to know what's going on.
Where were you? Were you okay?

00:06:21.133 --> 00:06:22.767
[ Laughter ]

00:06:22.767 --> 00:06:26.901
Did anyone help you?
What was this? What was this?

00:06:26.901 --> 00:06:29.701
-This is -- Okay.
[ Laughs ]

00:06:29.701 --> 00:06:32.400
I was 20 years old
in that picture.

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:35.934
I guess it was the year 2000.
I just moved to L.A.

00:06:35.934 --> 00:06:37.067
I knew I wanted to be an actor.

00:06:37.067 --> 00:06:40.534
I had no idea what to do
to become an actor.

00:06:40.534 --> 00:06:43.300
I had a car and that was it.
-That's a big deal.

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:46.300
Even having a car is a big deal.
-Yeah.

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:48.267
And I'd ask around
and my friend said,

00:06:48.267 --> 00:06:51.400
"What you need is something
called a headshot.

00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:53.200
And that's a picture
of your head."

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:54.334
[ Laughter ]

00:06:54.334 --> 00:06:55.534
"And then you send it
out to people.

00:06:55.534 --> 00:06:57.133
They're like,
'Hey, that's a good head.

00:06:57.133 --> 00:06:59.067
I'll look and meet him.'
You know?"

00:06:59.067 --> 00:07:00.667
-Yeah, I'll put that head
in my movie. Yeah.

00:07:00.667 --> 00:07:03.467
-Yeah. So I knew I needed
a headshot

00:07:03.467 --> 00:07:08.334
and I was in an area of
L.A. called West Hollywood,

00:07:08.334 --> 00:07:11.901
which you know West Hollywood.
It's a great part of Hollywood,

00:07:11.901 --> 00:07:13.934
predominantly gay area.
-Yeah.

00:07:13.934 --> 00:07:15.167
-Really kind of
a fabulous place.

00:07:15.167 --> 00:07:16.934
I was at the post office.

00:07:16.934 --> 00:07:19.000
There's a guy who is like
looking at me

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:23.000
for a long time
and he was like,

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:27.100
"You look familiar.
Have I shot you before?"

00:07:27.100 --> 00:07:29.434
And I was like,
"Oh, I've never been shot."

00:07:29.434 --> 00:07:30.934
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, yeah.

00:07:30.934 --> 00:07:33.601
-"Have you shot somebody?"

00:07:33.601 --> 00:07:35.200
I don't think
you've ever shot me.

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:36.601
-Either way, I'm fine.
-I would know.

00:07:36.601 --> 00:07:38.667
-I would never press charges.
-Yeah.

00:07:38.667 --> 00:07:40.901
-I'm fine.
-He was like,
"I'm a photographer."

00:07:40.901 --> 00:07:43.400
In my head, I'm like,
"Do you do headshots?"

00:07:43.400 --> 00:07:46.133
He's like, "Yeah. My apartment
is two blocks from here."

00:07:46.133 --> 00:07:48.234
[ Laughter ]

00:07:48.234 --> 00:07:50.300
I was like,
"Let's go, let's go."

00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:53.067
[ Laughter ]
So I walk over to the apartment.

00:07:53.067 --> 00:07:56.567
This guy's got like
a penthouse suite, really nice.

00:07:56.567 --> 00:07:58.934
He's like, "You probably need
to take a shower.

00:07:58.934 --> 00:08:01.400
You're a little messed up."

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:03.834
He was right. He was right.
I lived in the car.

00:08:03.834 --> 00:08:07.601
♪♪

00:08:07.601 --> 00:08:09.334
Hey, I'm just
painting a picture here.

00:08:09.334 --> 00:08:10.467
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:08:10.467 --> 00:08:13.767
-So I took the shower,
I got cleaned up.

00:08:13.767 --> 00:08:15.067
I did my hair,
as you can see.

00:08:15.067 --> 00:08:16.901
Like, you know,
picked it out a little.

00:08:16.901 --> 00:08:19.367
And then he was like,
"That shirt's not going to do.

00:08:19.367 --> 00:08:20.567
Here's one of mine."

00:08:20.567 --> 00:08:22.334
He gave me this shirt
that's in the picture.

00:08:22.334 --> 00:08:23.434
It's a white shirt.

00:08:23.434 --> 00:08:24.834
-That's his shirt?
-It's a nice shirt.

00:08:24.834 --> 00:08:26.734
I couldn't afford that shirt.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:08:26.734 --> 00:08:31.033
-I had that shirt.
And then he takes the pictures.

00:08:31.033 --> 00:08:33.934
He tells me what to do, tilt
my head, put my arm like this,

00:08:33.934 --> 00:08:36.100
takes the film out of the
camera, sticks it in the thing.

00:08:36.100 --> 00:08:38.567
He hands me three rolls
of camera film,

00:08:38.567 --> 00:08:40.634
which at the time
would have cost me like 400,

00:08:40.634 --> 00:08:44.133
500 bucks, you know, like head
shots are not inexpensive.

00:08:44.133 --> 00:08:45.868
And he was like,
"Good luck, kid."

00:08:45.868 --> 00:08:47.400
And I walked out of there

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:50.501
and then I decided
that this was the best one.

00:08:50.501 --> 00:08:53.434
[ Laughter and applause ]
-That's a great story.

00:08:53.434 --> 00:08:54.701
-Yeah.
-He's a good guy.

00:08:54.701 --> 00:08:56.300
-He is a good guy.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:56.300 --> 00:08:58.734
He's a good -- That's a good --
-So if you're watching,

00:08:58.734 --> 00:09:00.133
dude, if you remember,

00:09:00.133 --> 00:09:01.934
thank you, man. Thank you.
-You made his career, man.

00:09:01.934 --> 00:09:04.667
-You did. That got me on the WB.
That got me "Everwood."

00:09:04.667 --> 00:09:06.033
That was that headshot
that got me "Everwood."

00:09:06.033 --> 00:09:07.634
-Hey, that's awesome, buddy.
-Pretty cool.

00:09:07.634 --> 00:09:09.934
-Three, two, one.

00:09:09.934 --> 00:09:12.267
[ Camera shutter clicks ]

00:09:12.267 --> 00:09:14.834
And three, two, one.

00:09:14.834 --> 00:09:16.934
[ Camera shutter clicks ]

00:09:16.934 --> 00:09:19.234
-Three, two, one.

00:09:19.234 --> 00:09:20.701
[ Camera shutter clicks ]

00:09:20.701 --> 00:09:22.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:23.534 --> 00:09:25.801
-Ah! Oh, my God!

00:09:25.801 --> 00:09:27.767
-We should do a triple piggyback
in one of these.

00:09:27.767 --> 00:09:31.167
-And three, two, one.

00:09:31.167 --> 00:09:33.434
[ Camera shutter clicks ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:33.434 --> 00:09:35.901
-Dude, this next one,
we're getting lei'd.

