pocket money at 14.

00:12:15.801 --> 00:12:21.000
-Yeah. Yeah, it was good.
Well, here's a lesson I learned

00:12:21.000 --> 00:12:23.534
because the lady who
who owned the place was like,

00:12:23.534 --> 00:12:25.167
"Listen, if you ever
want to eat something,

00:12:25.167 --> 00:12:26.167
you just eat something.

00:12:26.167 --> 00:12:27.200
Just make sure
you write it down.

00:12:27.200 --> 00:12:29.167
We'll give it you for half price

00:12:29.167 --> 00:12:30.467
and then we'll just
take it out of your check."

00:12:30.467 --> 00:12:32.601
I was like, "Cool." So it was
kind of a credit system.

00:12:32.601 --> 00:12:34.467
-Yeah.
-And I worked there -- I think

00:12:34.467 --> 00:12:36.634
I got paid every two weeks
and I got my first check

00:12:36.634 --> 00:12:38.901
and they were like,
"Okay, let's just see.

00:12:38.901 --> 00:12:40.901
Here's what you got.
Oh, you owe us $80."

00:12:40.901 --> 00:12:42.501
[ Laughter ]

00:12:42.501 --> 00:12:43.434
I was like, "What?! How is that
possible?"

00:12:43.434 --> 00:12:45.767
-You owe them.
-I owed them $80.

00:12:45.767 --> 00:12:47.601
-You ate a lot of burgers.
-I ate a lot of stuff.

00:12:47.601 --> 00:12:49.300
-Yeah, that's good stuff.
-It was good stuff.

00:12:49.300 --> 00:12:51.067
-And how about your son now?
How old is your son now?

00:12:51.067 --> 00:12:52.434
-He's now two and a half.
-Two and a half.

00:12:52.434 --> 00:12:54.267
-And he's going to work, right?
Is he going to?

00:12:54.267 --> 00:12:55.901
-Yeah, we're trying to
get him jobs now.

00:12:55.901 --> 00:12:57.968
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, absolutely.

00:12:57.968 --> 00:12:59.100
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
What is he doing?

00:12:59.100 --> 00:13:00.667
