00:16:51.033 --> 00:16:53.934
My whole family. We always sing
karaoke at parties.

00:16:53.934 --> 00:16:57.200
-Do you have a go-to song?

00:16:57.200 --> 00:17:03.367
-Well, yeah, I did.
I had a go-to song that

00:17:03.367 --> 00:17:07.667
for a while I felt like
I murdered "Man in the Mirror."

00:17:07.667 --> 00:17:09.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:17:09.067 --> 00:17:10.467
-Michael Jackson?
-Michael Jackson.

00:17:10.467 --> 00:17:14.501
-That's a classic.
-I know. And then I realized...

00:17:14.501 --> 00:17:16.033
I have to tell you this story.

00:17:16.033 --> 00:17:19.567
The time I realized that
I don't murder Michael Jackson

00:17:19.567 --> 00:17:23.000
singing karaoke, I went
to -- I had killed it one week.

00:17:23.000 --> 00:17:26.133
I felt really good. I was like,
"Oh, that's my song."

00:17:26.133 --> 00:17:27.834
[ Laughter ]
-"I'm the next Michael Jackson."

00:17:27.834 --> 00:17:29.701
-"I can sing
'Man in the Mirror.'"

00:17:29.701 --> 00:17:32.868
-That's a tricky song.
-Very difficult,

00:17:32.868 --> 00:17:34.000
high degree of difficulty.

00:17:34.000 --> 00:17:35.400
But when you nail it,
you nail it.

00:17:35.400 --> 00:17:37.634
-Yeah, yeah.
-I was riding high on the wave

00:17:37.634 --> 00:17:40.367
of nailing "Man in the Mirror"
the week before.

00:17:40.367 --> 00:17:42.834
-Yeah.
-Went to the new karaoke bar.

00:17:42.834 --> 00:17:44.133
Met a girl.
-Oh, yeah.

00:17:44.133 --> 00:17:45.868
-Her name was Marina.

00:17:45.868 --> 00:17:49.300
Do you remember Marina?
I was flirting with her.

00:17:49.300 --> 00:17:51.267
I had "Man in the Mirror"
in my pocket.

00:17:51.267 --> 00:17:54.701
I knew I was going to kill it.
Put "Man in the Mirror" in.

00:17:54.701 --> 00:17:58.934
I got up on stage.
I said -- [ Laughs ]

00:17:58.934 --> 00:18:00.667
This is true, by the way.
I know I'm playing it up.

00:18:00.667 --> 00:18:03.601
But this was a really
a vulnerable moment for me.

00:18:03.601 --> 00:18:05.400
[ Laughter ]

00:18:05.400 --> 00:18:09.501
-Thank you for telling me this.
-I said...

00:18:09.501 --> 00:18:13.100
"This song is for Marina."
I swear to God.

00:18:13.100 --> 00:18:16.000
And then
the first note came out.

00:18:16.000 --> 00:18:18.234
And I didn't
realize there's different notes

00:18:18.234 --> 00:18:20.167
and different keys and stuff,

00:18:20.167 --> 00:18:22.534
and it just wasn't my key.
It wasn't my night.

00:18:22.534 --> 00:18:24.701
And it came out and it was like
I was like...

00:18:24.701 --> 00:18:26.601
[ Vocalizes ]

00:18:26.601 --> 00:18:28.801
♪ I'm gonna make a cha--♪

00:18:28.801 --> 00:18:31.067
Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:18:31.067 --> 00:18:32.367
-That's when you knew
you couldn't do it?

00:18:32.367 --> 00:18:35.200
-It didn't match, you know,
the sound didn't line up.

00:18:35.200 --> 00:18:36.534
-Oh, no.
-And I was like...

00:18:36.534 --> 00:18:38.033
♪ For once in my ♪

00:18:38.033 --> 00:18:39.501
"You suck!"

00:18:39.501 --> 00:18:41.100
[ Laughter ]

00:18:41.100 --> 00:18:42.834
And I just immediately
started sweating.

00:18:42.834 --> 00:18:45.133
Some guy yelled, "You suck."

00:18:45.133 --> 00:18:47.300
And I look and he was standing
right next to Marina.

00:18:47.300 --> 00:18:49.067
[ Audience ohhs ]

00:18:49.067 --> 00:18:50.834
And she left
with the "you suck" guy.

00:18:50.834 --> 00:18:52.167
[ Laughter ]

00:18:52.167 --> 00:18:54.801
[ Sad tuba ]

00:18:56.834 --> 00:18:59.367
I've never sang "Man
in the Mirror" since, man.

00:18:59.367 --> 00:19:00.634
It hurt. It hurt so bad.
-She left with the

00:19:00.634 --> 00:19:03.767
"you suck" guy.
Yeah. Well, no.

00:19:03.767 --> 00:19:06.901
How is the family?
How old is your son?

00:19:06.901 --> 00:19:08.767
-He turned four. He's about
almost four and a half.

00:19:08.767 --> 00:19:10.834
-Wow.
-Yeah, he's just great, man.

00:19:10.834 --> 00:19:12.033
-Isn't it cool?
-It is cool.

00:19:12.033 --> 00:19:13.467
-I mean,
I have three and a two,

00:19:13.467 --> 00:19:15.234
but it's just every day
is a new fun thing.

00:19:15.234 --> 00:19:16.968
Do they know that
you're in movies?

00:19:16.968 --> 00:19:18.434
Does he understand that yet?

00:19:18.434 --> 00:19:21.801
-He does, but he
doesn't, you know. It's not --

00:19:21.801 --> 00:19:24.100
The other day he went
to Universal Studios.

00:19:24.100 --> 00:19:27.167
You know, we were both
in "Jurassic World."

00:19:27.167 --> 00:19:30.033
Yes. And he --
-Number-one movie of all time.

00:19:30.033 --> 00:19:33.267
-He went to --
He went and they have a guy

00:19:33.267 --> 00:19:36.334
there dressed up like my
character from "Jurassic World."

00:19:36.334 --> 00:19:38.300
And he does the thing
with the raptors

00:19:38.300 --> 00:19:40.400
and they have like these
fake dinosaurs that come out

00:19:40.400 --> 00:19:42.501
and this guy pretends
to be that character

00:19:42.501 --> 00:19:45.167
and amuses the people
who come to Universal Studios.

00:19:45.167 --> 00:19:48.200
And he came home
and he's like, "Dad.

00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:50.601
I met the real
'Jurassic World' guy."

00:19:50.601 --> 00:19:53.434
[ Laughter ]

00:19:53.434 --> 00:19:58.000
-I'm like, "That guy? No!"
-"I'm the real guy."

00:19:58.000 --> 00:20:00.567
-He's like, "No, no, no, no, no.

00:20:00.567 --> 00:20:05.200
He doesn't do it on TV.
He's the real guy.

00:20:05.200 --> 00:20:08.801
I think it's the character
your guy is based on."

00:20:08.801 --> 00:20:10.501
-He met the real one, man.
-He met the real --

00:20:10.501 --> 00:20:11.868
He met the real
"Jurassic World" guy,

00:20:11.868 --> 00:20:13.334
so he was pretty thrilled.

00:20:13.334 --> 00:20:15.567
Yeah, same at Legoland.
He's like, "Dad, Emmet's here.

00:20:15.567 --> 00:20:17.334
The real Emmet, not you,
the real one."

00:20:17.334 --> 00:20:19.667
I'm like, "Come on, man."
-Come on, come on.

00:20:19.667 --> 00:20:21.100
Give Dad something.

00:20:21.100 --> 00:20:23.167
-I think he knows.
I think he's just being mean.

00:20:23.167 --> 00:20:24.234
-He's just playing with you.
Yeah.

00:20:24.234 --> 00:20:25.734
-[ Humming ]

00:20:25.734 --> 00:20:30.501
♪♪

00:20:30.501 --> 00:20:33.267
[ Laughter ]

00:20:33.267 --> 00:20:36.367
