-...not Eloise!

00:30:29.400 --> 00:30:31.000
-Eloise. Wait. That's beautiful.

00:30:31.000 --> 00:30:32.000
-Isn't that beautiful? Yeah.

00:30:32.000 --> 00:30:34.367
-You are now the father of
three.

00:30:34.367 --> 00:30:36.400
Does that ever sink in, bud?
-Wow.

00:30:36.400 --> 00:30:37.734
-This is -- You're a dad.

00:30:37.734 --> 00:30:39.000
-Whew!
-Yeah. I mean...

00:30:39.000 --> 00:30:41.033
-Yeah. Thank you.
-You're a fun dad.

00:30:41.033 --> 00:30:42.133
-I love it, man.

00:30:42.133 --> 00:30:43.901
Yeah, I have --
-You have a 10...

00:30:43.901 --> 00:30:46.601
-I got a 10-year-old, 2 1/2,
and 10 months.

00:30:46.601 --> 00:30:49.467
-Ooh!
-The 10-year-old is my son Jack.

00:30:49.467 --> 00:30:51.901
And then Lyla and Eloise,
the two girls.

00:30:51.901 --> 00:30:53.467
-How's Lyla doing?
-Oh, my gosh.

00:30:53.467 --> 00:30:55.100
She's -- She's the best.

00:30:55.100 --> 00:30:56.934
She's so girly. She's so cute.

00:30:56.934 --> 00:31:02.234
She loves dresses and bows
and all of the princessy stuff.

00:31:02.234 --> 00:31:03.467
Pink is her favorite color.

00:31:03.467 --> 00:31:05.467
And she loves to chat.
She's a real chatterbox.

00:31:05.467 --> 00:31:07.734
She'll talk -- She was talking
to my sister on FaceTime,

00:31:07.734 --> 00:31:10.634
and then my sister later said,
she goes, "Lyla is like

00:31:10.634 --> 00:31:16.000
the personification of a Mad Lib
'cause she knows all these

00:31:16.000 --> 00:31:18.734
words, but she doesn't quite
know how to really use them."

00:31:18.734 --> 00:31:21.534
So she'll -- The other day,
she said, "Daddy, Daddy.

00:31:21.534 --> 00:31:25.467
I'm going to Palm Beach
in two minutes!"

00:31:25.467 --> 00:31:27.000
[ Laughter ]

00:31:27.000 --> 00:31:28.868
I said, "You are?"
She said, "Yes.

00:31:28.868 --> 00:31:32.334
I'm going with Santa Claus.

00:31:32.334 --> 00:31:35.367
We are going to bring
all of the sand."

00:31:35.367 --> 00:31:36.767
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:31:36.767 --> 00:31:38.234
-I was like, "That's exactly
a Mad Lib."

00:31:38.234 --> 00:31:40.033
-Give me a noun. Give me a noun.

00:31:40.033 --> 00:31:41.300
-Give me an adjective.
-Yeah.

00:31:41.300 --> 00:31:43.000
And how's Grandpa?

00:31:43.000 --> 00:31:44.834
Arnold Schwarzenegger
is your grandpa.

00:31:44.834 --> 00:31:46.267
-Yeah. He goes by "Opa."

00:31:46.267 --> 00:31:48.300
-Oh.
-You know, he's Austrian.

00:31:48.300 --> 00:31:51.400
German. "Opa" is "grandfather"
in German.

00:31:51.400 --> 00:31:52.467
So he goes by "Opa."

00:31:52.467 --> 00:31:54.133
-[ As Arnold ]
Did he have a cigar?

00:31:54.133 --> 00:31:55.734
-Oh. [ Laughs ]

00:31:55.734 --> 00:31:57.400
-Did you have a cigar with him?
-Yes. Yes.

00:31:57.400 --> 00:31:59.334
-Yes. You had the cigar?
-Yeah.

00:31:59.334 --> 00:32:00.567
-[ Normal voice ]
He loves his cigar.

00:32:00.567 --> 00:32:01.901
-He loves his cigar.
-He came on the show.

00:32:01.901 --> 00:32:03.033
He taught me
how to smoke a cigar.

00:32:03.033 --> 00:32:04.534
-Yeah, he kind of taught me,
too.

00:32:04.534 --> 00:32:05.968
I mean, there's nothing manlier

00:32:05.968 --> 00:32:08.534
than Arnold Schwarzenegger
smoking a cigar.

00:32:08.534 --> 00:32:13.801
And when you're part of, you
know, bringing his granddaughter

00:32:13.801 --> 00:32:16.100
into the world, he comes
and he brings you a cigar

00:32:16.100 --> 00:32:17.534
and he's like, "Let's go out
and smoke these."

00:32:17.534 --> 00:32:18.701
And I was like, "Okay,"

00:32:18.701 --> 00:32:20.434
but I have asthma,
so I don't like cigars.

00:32:20.434 --> 00:32:22.234
And I was like,
"You got it, Arnold."

00:32:22.234 --> 00:32:23.400
And Katherine's like,
"What are you doing?"

00:32:23.400 --> 00:32:24.934
I was like, "I'm fine.
I'm gonna be okay."

00:32:24.934 --> 00:32:26.801
And so I go and I smoke
the cigar

00:32:26.801 --> 00:32:27.801
and I'm like, "This is good.

00:32:27.801 --> 00:32:29.534
[ Coughs ]
Hmm. Oh, yeah.

00:32:29.534 --> 00:32:30.934
Cohiba? Nice."

00:32:30.934 --> 00:32:32.934
And then woke up the next day.

00:32:32.934 --> 00:32:34.601
Massive lung infection, but...

00:32:34.601 --> 00:32:35.701
[ Laughter ]

00:32:35.701 --> 00:32:37.834
Worth it.
-You always have to --

00:32:37.834 --> 00:32:39.901
If Arnold says,
"Let's smoke a cigar..."

00:32:39.901 --> 00:32:41.067
-You go, "Okay."
-Let's do it. Yeah.

00:32:41.067 --> 00:32:42.267
You go, "Yeah."

00:32:42.267 --> 00:32:43.767
-There's peer pressure,

00:32:43.767 --> 00:32:45.300
and then there's...
-Arnold Schwarzenegger.

00:32:45.300 --> 00:32:46.367
-...Arnold Schwarzenegger
pressure.

00:32:46.367 --> 00:32:47.868
-No, you do whatever --
He came on.

00:32:47.868 --> 00:32:50.801
I said I want to understand it
and how to do it and everything,

00:32:50.801 --> 00:32:52.601
because I smoked
a couple of cigars.

00:32:52.601 --> 00:32:55.534
I don't know when. And I'm
like -- You bite the end off

00:32:55.534 --> 00:32:57.400
and then you, like,
lick the side.

00:32:57.400 --> 00:32:59.100
He goes [As Arnold] "You don't
bite and lick it.

00:32:59.100 --> 00:33:01.567
What are you talking about?
You don't lick the cigar!

00:33:01.567 --> 00:33:02.801
You don't lick it and bite it!"

00:33:02.801 --> 00:33:04.601
[ Normal voice ]
I go, "I think I did."

00:33:04.601 --> 00:33:05.934
He's like, "No!" He goes,

00:33:05.934 --> 00:33:07.234
[As Arnold] "Next time I'm in
town, I'll teach you.

00:33:07.234 --> 00:33:09.434
I'll take you to a cigar bar,
and I'll teach you how."

00:33:09.434 --> 00:33:10.968
[ Normal voice ] I go --
And he's a man of his word.

00:33:10.968 --> 00:33:12.334
Called me on the phone.
-No.

00:33:12.334 --> 00:33:15.334
-Said, "Jimmy, it's Arnold.
I'm going to a cigar bar."

00:33:15.334 --> 00:33:18.901
And I was with -- I was with
Drew Barrymore and my wife,

00:33:18.901 --> 00:33:20.567
and I go, "Do you guys want to
go to a cigar bar

00:33:20.567 --> 00:33:22.434
with Arnold Schwarzenegger?"
They're like, "Let's do it."

00:33:22.434 --> 00:33:24.367
We showed up,
and we all smoked cigars.

00:33:24.367 --> 00:33:25.434
-Come on.
-It was the best.

00:33:25.434 --> 00:33:27.467
Love that dude. Congrats, Opa.

00:33:27.467 --> 00:33:28.901
Opa?
-Opa Arnold.

00:33:28.901 --> 00:33:30.000
-Congratulations, Opa.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:33:30.000 --> 00:33:31.400
-Stogies.

00:33:31.400 --> 00:33:32.601
-Congrats to you and Katherine.

00:33:32.601 --> 00:33:34.234
-Thanks, man. Thank you.
Yeah, we're blessed.

00:33:34.234 --> 00:33:36.067
We feel very blessed.
-Good, nice parents.

00:33:36.067 --> 00:33:37.634
I want to talk
"Super Mario Bros."

00:33:37.634 --> 00:33:39.100
because that is --
That's the jam.

00:33:39.100 --> 00:33:40.567
I'm excited about
this Wednesday.

00:33:40.567 --> 00:33:42.267
-Let's go.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:33:42.267 --> 00:33:43.567
-I'm excited.
-Go see it.

00:33:43.567 --> 00:33:44.767
-You're Mario.

00:33:44.767 --> 00:33:46.200
-I'm Mario.
I'm the voice of Mario.

00:33:46.200 --> 00:33:47.834
-So what happens when you get
the phone call and they're like,

00:33:47.834 --> 00:33:50.667
"Hey, would you like to be
this iconic..."

00:33:50.667 --> 00:33:52.501
-I'm like, "Pfft. No."
[ Laughter ]

00:33:52.501 --> 00:33:53.868
-Yeah. Exactly.

00:33:53.868 --> 00:33:56.100
-I was like, "Oh, my God!
Really?!"

00:33:56.100 --> 00:33:58.467
Yeah, I mean, you get that call.

00:33:58.467 --> 00:34:01.067
And it's just really exciting
because, I mean, if you think

00:34:01.067 --> 00:34:03.767
about it, all the IP that's out
there, anything that has reach,

00:34:03.767 --> 00:34:05.100
it's already been remade.

00:34:05.100 --> 00:34:07.601
It's already been turned into
a TV show or a movie.

00:34:07.601 --> 00:34:09.200
And for some reason,
the Super Mario Bros.

00:34:09.200 --> 00:34:11.400
hasn't been a movie
for almost 30 years.

00:34:11.400 --> 00:34:13.300
And it's because I think the
folks at Nintendo just didn't

00:34:13.300 --> 00:34:15.567
want to give anybody the
permission to make the movie,

00:34:15.567 --> 00:34:17.167
and so finally they made...

00:34:17.167 --> 00:34:19.300
-Oh, Illumination is --
-Illumination, you know --

00:34:19.300 --> 00:34:20.901
"Despicable Me,"
"Secret Life of Pets."

00:34:20.901 --> 00:34:22.234
-"Minions." Brilliant.
-"Minions."

00:34:22.234 --> 00:34:25.234
Incredible studio.
And so they partnered up

00:34:25.234 --> 00:34:27.367
and they decided that they were
going to make this movie.

00:34:27.367 --> 00:34:30.067
And so when something like that
comes around, it's just like --

00:34:30.067 --> 00:34:32.400
you're so blessed, so honored
to do it, I mean, for me...

00:34:32.400 --> 00:34:34.868
-It's fantastic.
It's gonna crush, buddy.

00:34:34.868 --> 00:34:36.234
And, you know, I was thinking
about you

00:34:36.234 --> 00:34:37.801
because I was watching it,
and there's a lot of action.

00:34:37.801 --> 00:34:40.267
There's a lot of action
in this movie.

00:34:40.267 --> 00:34:44.667
And I could just kind of hear
you -- a lot of grunting by you.

00:34:44.667 --> 00:34:45.868
-Yes.
-Going like...

00:34:45.868 --> 00:34:47.367
[ Grunting ]

00:34:47.367 --> 00:34:49.901
And I go -- I was like -- "Oh,
maybe Chris will bring footage,"

00:34:49.901 --> 00:34:52.667
of you doing those grunts
when you come on the show.

00:34:52.667 --> 00:34:54.033
I just want to see you in
the sound booth going like...

00:34:54.033 --> 00:34:55.767
[ Both grunting ]

00:34:55.767 --> 00:34:57.534
-Well, you know, here's
an interesting thing

00:34:57.534 --> 00:34:59.467
about that, actually.

00:34:59.467 --> 00:35:02.033
Usually the effort sounds you do
at the end of the session.

00:35:02.033 --> 00:35:04.367
You probably do like one or two
sessions a month over the course

00:35:04.367 --> 00:35:06.267
of a couple years to voice one
of these movies.

00:35:06.267 --> 00:35:08.934
And at the end, because
the efforts and the grunts

00:35:08.934 --> 00:35:10.667
and the screaming, that really
takes it out of your voice,

00:35:10.667 --> 00:35:12.000
they save that for the end.

00:35:12.000 --> 00:35:15.267
But here's an interesting
little tidbit.

00:35:15.267 --> 00:35:18.267
In a -- What makes physical
comedy work in

00:35:18.267 --> 00:35:20.367
like a "Tom and Jerry"
or a "Super Mario Bros."

00:35:20.367 --> 00:35:25.534
is when a character falls
a long way and hits,

00:35:25.534 --> 00:35:27.300
they don't die, right?

00:35:27.300 --> 00:35:29.467
If they died, it would --
If Tom and Jerry --

00:35:29.467 --> 00:35:33.067
If, like, Road Runner -- If,
like, the anvil hit his head

00:35:33.067 --> 00:35:34.467
and there's freaking brains
everywhere...

00:35:34.467 --> 00:35:35.567
-No, no, no, no, no.
That'd be terrible.

00:35:35.567 --> 00:35:37.200
[ Laughter ]
-Be like, "Oh, my God!"

00:35:37.200 --> 00:35:38.767
That'd be bad, right?
-Terrible idea. Terrible.

00:35:38.767 --> 00:35:43.868
-So in order to let kids know
that the character's not dead...

00:35:43.868 --> 00:35:46.033
-Yes.
-...you have to do an,

00:35:46.033 --> 00:35:48.734
"I'm okay, I'm alive" sigh.

00:35:48.734 --> 00:35:50.767
"I'm hurt, not injured" sigh.

00:35:50.767 --> 00:35:52.901
So it's like this.
You're like, "Aaaaaah!"

00:35:52.901 --> 00:35:54.734
Unh!

00:35:54.734 --> 00:35:56.200
Uhh...

00:35:56.200 --> 00:35:58.834
-Yeah!
[ Applause ]

00:35:58.834 --> 00:35:59.968
-Without that...

00:35:59.968 --> 00:36:01.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:36:01.334 --> 00:36:03.567
-It just goes, hey, it's a joke,
everybody.

00:36:03.567 --> 00:36:06.000
-Kids will be like,
"Mario is dead!

00:36:06.000 --> 00:36:08.767
Mario fell to his death, Dad!"
-That's so funny.

00:36:08.767 --> 00:36:11.167
It's so well-done.
It's such a great cast.

00:36:11.167 --> 00:36:13.467
Everyone's so talented and good.
A lot of fun people.

00:36:19.601 --> 00:36:20.667
-Good luck.

00:36:23.133 --> 00:36:24.434
-Super Mario Bros.

00:36:24.434 --> 00:36:26.100
-Boom! Let's see the answer!

00:36:27.033 --> 00:36:30.200
[ Ding! ]
Yes! Super Mario Bros.!

00:36:30.200 --> 00:36:31.834
-Wow.
-Wow.

00:36:31.834 --> 00:36:33.934
That was a hard question.
-How was that a hard question?

00:36:33.934 --> 00:36:35.267
-James. Oh, yo!

00:36:35.267 --> 00:36:36.601
[ Mario power-up sound plays ]
-[ Laughs ]

00:36:36.601 --> 00:36:38.033
-How was that a hard question?

00:36:38.033 --> 00:36:39.667
It's basically every video game
right there.

00:36:39.667 --> 00:36:41.434
-Right. It was hard.
That was a difficult question.

00:36:41.434 --> 00:36:43.000
-Alright.
-Now, here's your question.

00:36:43.000 --> 00:36:44.934
-Yeah. Oh, good luck.

00:36:44.934 --> 00:36:46.300
-Good luck, James.
-Yeah.

00:36:49.901 --> 00:36:52.100
♪♪

00:36:52.100 --> 00:36:53.734
[ Laughter ]

00:36:53.734 --> 00:36:54.934
Who's the creator?

00:36:54.934 --> 00:36:56.467
-I mean, I'm a Nintendo nerd.

00:36:56.467 --> 00:36:58.534
I'm going to say Miyamoto?

00:36:58.534 --> 00:36:59.634
-Judges?

00:36:59.634 --> 00:37:00.934
[ Drum roll ]

00:37:00.934 --> 00:37:02.801
[ Ding! ]
Yes!

00:37:02.801 --> 00:37:04.267
Shigeru Miyamoto.

00:37:04.267 --> 00:37:07.834
Chris. Ready?

00:37:07.834 --> 00:37:09.367
[ Mario power-up sound plays ]

00:37:09.367 --> 00:37:12.267
[ Grunts ]

00:37:12.267 --> 00:37:13.934
He's more man than you. Okay.

00:37:13.934 --> 00:37:15.834
[ Laughter ]

00:37:15.834 --> 00:37:17.834
-What?
-Wow.

00:37:17.834 --> 00:37:19.901
-Hurt my leg.
-My God.

00:37:19.901 --> 00:37:21.801
-Oy!
-God.

00:37:21.801 --> 00:37:24.234
-[ Laughing ]

00:37:24.234 --> 00:37:25.534
Chris?
-Yes.

00:37:29.901 --> 00:37:31.100
-This is a hard one.

00:37:31.100 --> 00:37:33.734
-Pfft!
-Travel across 1800s America?

00:37:33.734 --> 00:37:35.901
-Yeah.
-Okay, now I'm going to phone

00:37:35.901 --> 00:37:37.968
a friend on this -- uh, myself.

00:37:37.968 --> 00:37:39.467
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:37:39.467 --> 00:37:42.300
-Hello? Yeah, uh, is that --

00:37:42.300 --> 00:37:43.968
I think it's, uh, Oregon Trail?

00:37:43.968 --> 00:37:45.734
-Let's see.
Let's see the answer.

00:37:45.734 --> 00:37:47.467
[ Ding! ]
Oregon Trail! Yes!

00:37:47.467 --> 00:37:49.367
-Hey! I played that at school.

00:37:49.367 --> 00:37:51.634
-Oh, my God.
-I played that in school.

00:37:51.634 --> 00:37:53.400
-You died of dysentery.
You got a snake bite.

00:37:53.400 --> 00:37:54.868
-Oh, yeah, you died
of a snake bite.

00:37:54.868 --> 00:37:56.667
-Ready, Jimmy? You're going up.

00:37:56.667 --> 00:37:59.634
[ Mario power-up sound plays ]
Ohhhhh, my gosh!

00:37:59.634 --> 00:38:02.667
Okay, Jimmy, next question is
for you.

00:38:08.434 --> 00:38:10.133
You know this.

00:38:10.133 --> 00:38:12.300
-Well, first, I want to give
a shout-out to my...

00:38:12.300 --> 00:38:14.033
-[ Laughs ]

00:38:14.033 --> 00:38:16.434
-...my buddy Weasel back at home
in Boston.

00:38:16.434 --> 00:38:17.801
You know I love you, Weaz.

00:38:17.801 --> 00:38:20.834
Uh, you're talking about
EA Sports. Come on, dude.

00:38:20.834 --> 00:38:21.934
-All right, let's see
the answer.

00:38:21.934 --> 00:38:23.000
-Electronic Arts.

00:38:23.000 --> 00:38:24.634
-Yeah!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:38:24.634 --> 00:38:26.167
Okay, Chris.

00:38:26.167 --> 00:38:27.534
Oh, my God. So close.
[ Mario power-up sound plays ]

00:38:27.534 --> 00:38:29.133
-Aaaah!

00:38:29.133 --> 00:38:30.968
-♪ So close ♪

00:38:30.968 --> 00:38:33.000
-If it's in the game --
-Alright, Chris.

00:38:33.000 --> 00:38:34.734
Next question is to you.
-Okay.

00:38:42.501 --> 00:38:44.234
-[ Laughs ]
-Not What, like his name.

00:38:44.234 --> 00:38:46.267
What is his name?
It's not What.

00:38:46.267 --> 00:38:47.934
-Blinky.
-Inky.

00:38:47.934 --> 00:38:49.133
-Inky.
-Pinky and...

00:38:49.133 --> 00:38:50.534
-Pinky and...

00:38:50.534 --> 00:38:51.734
[ Drum roll ]

00:38:51.734 --> 00:38:53.300
It's got to rhy-- I don't know.

00:38:53.300 --> 00:38:54.834
I'm going to have
to take a guess.

00:38:54.834 --> 00:38:56.634
Uh, Juanita?

00:38:56.634 --> 00:38:57.801
-[ Laughs ]
-Juanita.

00:38:57.801 --> 00:38:58.868
[ Sad tuba ]

00:38:58.868 --> 00:39:00.400
Jimmy, do you know the answer?

00:39:00.400 --> 00:39:02.100
-I do, but it's not --
It doesn't rhyme.

00:39:02.100 --> 00:39:04.567
It's like Gary or something.
Or Paul or something.

00:39:04.567 --> 00:39:05.634
-Let's see.
Judges, let's see the answer.

00:39:05.634 --> 00:39:06.734
-If it's Gary,
I'm gonna be upset.

00:39:06.734 --> 00:39:08.367
-It's Clyde!

00:39:08.367 --> 00:39:10.601
Oh, Chris. One more.
Ohh, so close!

00:39:10.601 --> 00:39:12.601
[ Mario power-up sound plays ]

00:39:12.601 --> 00:39:14.334
-Oh, my God.
-All right, Jimmy.

00:39:14.334 --> 00:39:15.467
-[ Laughs ]

00:39:15.467 --> 00:39:16.767
-Next question is for you.

00:39:16.767 --> 00:39:19.467
-Yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes!

00:39:19.467 --> 00:39:20.634
Clyde.

00:39:23.834 --> 00:39:26.133
Yes. Yes.

00:39:26.133 --> 00:39:27.234
-...not Trump...
-Q-Bert.

00:39:27.234 --> 00:39:28.501
Who changes co--

00:39:28.501 --> 00:39:30.167
You're just gonna jump
right on it? Q-Bert?

00:39:30.167 --> 00:39:31.601
Let's see the answer.

00:39:32.367 --> 00:39:33.734
[ Ding! ]
Yes!

00:39:33.734 --> 00:39:35.300
Q-Bert.

00:39:35.300 --> 00:39:36.734
♪♪

00:39:36.734 --> 00:39:37.901
[ Mario power-up sound plays ]

00:39:37.901 --> 00:39:39.100
[ Laughing ]

00:39:39.100 --> 00:39:41.267
Oh, my gosh. Chris.

00:39:41.267 --> 00:39:43.000
-Are you kidding me?
-Next question is for you.

00:39:43.000 --> 00:39:44.534
-What, does his head gotta go
in the pipe?!

00:39:44.534 --> 00:39:45.834
-Well, he's got to go
in the pipe.

00:39:45.834 --> 00:39:47.300
And that's not -- Trust me.
-For heaven's sakes.

00:39:47.300 --> 00:39:49.033
-You don't want to get that
dumped on your head.

00:39:49.033 --> 00:39:50.501
[ Balloon pops ]
Oh!

00:39:50.501 --> 00:39:51.667
[ Laughter ]

00:39:51.667 --> 00:39:54.467
[ Mario coins rapidly dinging ]

00:39:54.467 --> 00:39:55.734
-Wow!

00:39:55.734 --> 00:39:58.234
His laughter! His laughter!

00:39:58.234 --> 00:40:00.133
His laughter,
that's what got him!

00:40:00.133 --> 00:40:01.567
He's a good sport.

00:40:01.567 --> 00:40:02.968
-Let's see a slow-mo of that!

00:40:02.968 --> 00:40:04.534
[ Cheers and applause ]
Oh!

00:40:04.534 --> 00:40:05.801
-Chris Pratt, everybody.

